{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030332-how-do-the-seers-defend-new-york","id":1030332,"title":"How do the Seers defend New York?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-11T17:16:32-08:00","id":1030332,"title":"How do the Seers defend New York?","content":"So, I'm well aware that the Seers took over Manhattan in the wake of some big crisis which necessitated the Pentacle Orders and the Seers working together, and that there's some big Detente regarding Pentacle mages not being allowed to use Magic within Manhattan, and that there's some kind of ward or protection that enforces this somehow.<br /> <br /> My question is; How? What's the nature of this protection? How does it work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:20:48-08:00","id":1030337,"title":"","content":"Like, can Seers just have 10 mages of each Arcanum, looking in 8 hour shifts over Manhattan and counterspelling any breach? It's 30 persons tops and it's seems like they would do the thing like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:40:57-08:00","id":1030350,"title":"","content":"If you can wait a year or two for Tome of the Pentacle, you might get an official answer when NYC gets a writeup.<br /> <br /> I think the crisis that brought them together involved super bad mass-murder resonance being pumped into the ley lines. Building on that, maybe the Seers have taken control of and weaponized the ley lines of Manhattan? I can imagine a complex Space/Prime/Fate spell on the lines that lets the Seers establish a Key where only authorized users can cast spells on the island, and any non-Keyed activity sends a warning up the hypersensitive lines to the nearest Node.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:08:37-08:00","id":1030439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030332-how-do-the-seers-defend-new-york?p=1030337#post1030337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, can Seers just have 10 mages of each Arcanum, looking in 8 hour shifts over Manhattan and counterspelling any breach? It's 30 persons tops and it's seems like they would do the thing like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Seers are ambitious and self-serving by nature; they do the bidding of the Exarchs in exchange for power, but I don't see them settling for a 9-5 grind. Setting up some kind of massive ward to interfere with spellcasting on Manhattan Island might be doable, though. A piece of Hunter fiction suggests that a pylon in Philadelphia was known for doing just that kind of thing on a smaller scale, though it eventually came back to bite them when they were ambushed during a meeting in an apartment that was warded such that only their most senior (and paranoid) member could actually cast spells.<br /> <br /> Alternately, they could have worked out some kind of Manhattan-specific Mystery that they can exploit to keep themselves in power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-12-2017, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T03:09:40-08:00","id":1030493,"title":"","content":"Manhattan's Mystery is that the city rearranges itself, but the changes are covered by Quiescence so noone remembers that their building used to be three blocks over, etc.<br /> <br /> The Seers figured out how to control it to some extent (there may be some intelligence behind it, like the mother of all Genius Locii). <br /> Pentacle mages can go into Manhattan and cast spells just fine. But the Hallows refuse them Mana, and attempts to establish Sancta are literally fought off by the city itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T03:13:05-08:00","id":1030495,"title":"","content":"I'm now imagining fighting a Seer Mastigos in Manhatten basically being one of those Inception-rip-off scenes from Doctor Strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T03:26:24-08:00","id":1030499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030332-how-do-the-seers-defend-new-york?p=1030495#post1030495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now imagining fighting a Seer Mastigos in Manhatten basically being one of those Inception-rip-off scenes from Doctor Strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <b>Doctor Strange</b> was taking place in NYC - maybe it's a <i>film</i> that is rip-off of real history of Manhattan... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-12-2017, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T13:14:24-08:00","id":1030745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030332-how-do-the-seers-defend-new-york?p=1030493#post1030493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manhattan's Mystery is that the city rearranges itself, but the changes are covered by Quiescence so noone remembers that their building used to be three blocks over, etc.<br /> <br /> The Seers figured out how to control it to some extent (there may be some intelligence behind it, like the mother of all Genius Locii).<br /> Pentacle mages can go into Manhattan and cast spells just fine. But the Hallows refuse them Mana, and attempts to establish Sancta are literally fought off by the city itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manhattan's Mystery, you say? Do all (or at least most) densely populated places have some kind of thematic mystery that permeates the whole area? That certainly seems to be the case for the cities showcased in the book... could be a fun idea for a brainstorming thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030332-how-do-the-seers-defend-new-york?p=1030499#post1030499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As <b>Doctor Strange</b> was taking place in NYC - maybe it's a <i>film</i> that is rip-off of real history of Manhattan... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine that being the Libertine take on it. In fact, I bet there's a Libertine in Jersey City or somewhere who's currently picking apart that movie frame-by-frame and learning all he can about the production history in the hopes of gaining some insight into how the Seers control Manhattan's mutable landscape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-12-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T14:11:25-08:00","id":1030784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030332-how-do-the-seers-defend-new-york?p=1030495#post1030495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now imagining fighting a Seer Mastigos in Manhatten basically being one of those Inception-rip-off scenes from Doctor Strange.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was hardly a rip-off of Inception. Inception went half-Escher, Dr. Strange went full-Escher.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030332-how-do-the-seers-defend-new-york?p=1030745#post1030745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manhattan's Mystery, you say? Do all (or at least most) densely populated places have some kind of thematic mystery that permeates the whole area? That certainly seems to be the case for the cities showcased in the book... could be a fun idea for a brainstorming thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they just make them up on a city by city basis. The mystery of Copenhagen could be that water no longer flows past its islands but stagnates and grows weirdly mutated fish that come out of the water smelling like surstromming. In Amsterdam coffee shop visitors unintentionally trace Atlantean runes in the paths they walk after smoking a particular strain of weed that's not on any store's menu. In Paris there is an arrogance league, where the 100 most arrogant Parisians are selected and taken to a special area by the subway where they have to insult each other until only one person remains as king shit of shit mountain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","user":"logos","date":". 01-12-2017, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T23:24:13-08:00","id":1031021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030332-how-do-the-seers-defend-new-york?p=1030745#post1030745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manhattan's Mystery, you say? Do all (or at least most) densely populated places have some kind of thematic mystery that permeates the whole area? That certainly seems to be the case for the cities showcased in the book... could be a fun idea for a brainstorming thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of, but it's less that large concentrations of people in urban areas inherently give rise to complex Mysteries as an in-character thing, and more that if you as an ST are running a game you should plan for an interesting Mystery to build a setting around. To the extent that there are people who want to run a Mage game in Lagos, there's probably a massive Atlantean temple complex there or a haunted weather pattern or the Underworld is all screwy or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}